  3+  81BD              ; Unpacking a message.  See doc/textos.md.
  4+  81BD              ;
  5+  81BD              ; A code below the first pair is a character; anything else stands for two
  6+  81BD              ; codes, and those may stand for two more.  Walking that needs a stack, so the
  7+  81BD              ; machine's own is used by letting the routine call itself: the deepest any of
  8+  81BD              ; the eight adventures went was ten levels, which is forty bytes.
  9+  81BD              ;
 10+  81BD              ; A message unpacks on its own, touching nothing before it, which is what lets
 11+  81BD              ; the interpreter print message 137 and only that one.
 12+  81BD
